{:edb/db-before-t 1317 :edb/db-after-t 1318 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534630 50 #inst "2026-10-08T02:55:43.892Z" 13194139534630 true] [17592186105655 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299797 13194139534630 true] [17592186105655 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299804 13194139534630 true] [17592186105655 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299818 13194139534630 true] [17592186105677 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299811 13194139534630 true] [17592186106030 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534630 true] [17592186106030 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nGiven that $a \\cdot b =-8$, find the angle between $a = ⟨2t, 2t⟩$ and $b = ⟨4,-2⟩$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." 13194139534630 false] [17592186106030 1100 "Given that $a\\cdot b=-8$, find the angle between $a=⟨2t,2t⟩$ and $b=⟨4,-2⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." 13194139534630 true] [17592186106030 1145 "First, since $a\\cdot b=-8$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-8 \\\\ 2t\\cdot 4+2t\\cdot (-2) & =-8 \\\\ 8t-4t & =-8 \\\\ 4t & =-8 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨2(-2),\\,2(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8}{\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-4)^{2}}\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{4\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}})≈{108.4}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299797 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299798 13194139534630 true] [17592186299797 1089 "q-101507" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299797 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534630 true] [17592186299797 1100 "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(3,3,-5)$, $Q(4,2,-3)$, and $R(7,5,-3).$" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299797 1113 #uuid "9c69e64f-0c1c-5d77-8cc6-1e79f32671e2" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299797 1145 "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨3,3,-5⟩,\\,q=⟨4,2,-3⟩,\\,r=⟨7,5,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨4,2,-3⟩-⟨3,3,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨7,5,-3⟩-⟨3,3,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})={60}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299798 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299799 13194139534630 true] [17592186299798 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299800 13194139534630 true] [17592186299798 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299801 13194139534630 true] [17592186299798 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299802 13194139534630 true] [17592186299798 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299803 13194139534630 true] [17592186299798 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534630 true] [17592186299798 1041 "selection" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299798 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299799 13194139534630 true] [17592186299798 1110 #uuid "2c14524a-0a65-5ba4-8f11-cae23eb5c03c" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299799 1034 "{60}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299799 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299799 1111 #uuid "82833760-4058-5477-be97-714836c7a619" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299800 1034 "{90}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299800 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299800 1111 #uuid "bc1a7e92-4556-5b5d-b92d-34759ce02755" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299801 1034 "{180}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299801 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299801 1111 #uuid "3c740ec8-3370-577f-8106-c8f155d23e0d" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299802 1034 "{45}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299802 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299802 1111 #uuid "ba7f1739-0235-568b-bbbb-832a0aa10a42" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299803 1034 "{30}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299803 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299803 1111 #uuid "1bb3ced9-0e15-51fe-9c7a-fd0e314ab216" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299804 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299805 13194139534630 true] [17592186299804 1089 "q-101509" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299804 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534630 true] [17592186299804 1100 "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(-5,1,3)$, $Q(-3,-1,2)$, and $R(-5,2,4).$" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299804 1113 #uuid "391b39e3-9f88-5170-837b-46afd5273322" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299804 1145 "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨-5,1,3⟩,\\,q=⟨-3,-1,2⟩,\\,r=⟨-5,2,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨-3,-1,2⟩-⟨-5,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨-5,2,4⟩-⟨-5,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={135}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299805 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299806 13194139534630 true] [17592186299805 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299807 13194139534630 true] [17592186299805 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299808 13194139534630 true] [17592186299805 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299809 13194139534630 true] [17592186299805 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299810 13194139534630 true] [17592186299805 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534630 true] [17592186299805 1041 "selection" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299805 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299809 13194139534630 true] [17592186299805 1110 #uuid "287483dc-6fb7-561c-9040-69de63053737" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299806 1034 "{150}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299806 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299806 1111 #uuid "a242ad42-2fc2-5601-ba9a-edbad9b26204" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299807 1034 "{90}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299807 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299807 1111 #uuid "d8bd10ce-d813-586d-8e95-71dd6d661d69" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299808 1034 "{180}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299808 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299808 1111 #uuid "82e379ab-9ab5-51e8-a2ed-e84d02c3bc54" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299809 1034 "{135}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299809 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299809 1111 #uuid "987b5ab8-6bd3-50bd-b1b7-d7b3e0ddc4bb" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299810 1034 "{120}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299810 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299810 1111 #uuid "b26c1645-bf58-50ba-adf4-6611a5d15f6b" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299811 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299812 13194139534630 true] [17592186299811 1089 "q-125078" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299811 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534630 true] [17592186299811 1100 "Given that $a\\cdot b=-9$, find the angle between $a=⟨-2t,3t⟩$ and $b=⟨3,1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." 13194139534630 true] [17592186299811 1113 #uuid "47778997-e90f-5f7d-b2f9-574ccbc3b4d8" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299811 1145 "First, since $a\\cdot b=-9$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-9 \\\\ -2t\\cdot 3+3t\\cdot 1 & =-9 \\\\ -6t+3t & =-9 \\\\ -3t & =-9 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨-2(3),\\,3(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9}{\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{9}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{117}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{3\\sqrt{13}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{130}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{130}})≈{105.3}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299813 13194139534630 true] [17592186299812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299814 13194139534630 true] [17592186299812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299815 13194139534630 true] [17592186299812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299816 13194139534630 true] [17592186299812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299817 13194139534630 true] [17592186299812 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534630 true] [17592186299812 1041 "selection" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299812 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299813 13194139534630 true] [17592186299812 1110 #uuid "0f7c4f24-38ef-52a3-a79c-0c6c63b4ef63" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299813 1034 "{105.3}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299813 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299813 1111 #uuid "6a441dca-25da-57b4-b90c-27dfb3b87a19" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299814 1034 "{123.2}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299814 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299814 1111 #uuid "13964d5a-9967-5ef6-9b12-d693f54cae14" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299815 1034 "{100.5}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299815 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299815 1111 #uuid "b0ae7195-cfbc-5e22-944d-afe431f5cdca" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299816 1034 "{95.9}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299816 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299816 1111 #uuid "bda0f309-e6e5-5017-8ce0-b80ffba45cd7" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299817 1034 "{115.2}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299817 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299817 1111 #uuid "86e52145-75b1-5720-bbb3-99b6a2e78b24" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299818 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299819 13194139534630 true] [17592186299818 1089 "q-69833" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299818 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534630 true] [17592186299818 1100 "Find $∠XZY$ given the points $X(-1,0,3)$, $Y(-2,2,3)$, and $Z(-2,-1,3).$" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299818 1113 #uuid "6dd6f17b-7e99-5c2a-8be5-e863ab15158a" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299818 1145 "Note that the position vectors of the points $X$, $Y$, $Z$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,y=⟨-2,2,3⟩,\\,z=⟨-2,-1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△XYZ$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠XZY=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/assets/87453fecb9da6b9e673ab5a85a289a3fac73f4fb90fc8f1b33e7c0a80b1ea77f.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ZX} & =x-z \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,3⟩-⟨-2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{ZY} & =y-z \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,3⟩-⟨-2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ZX}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{ZY}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ZX}||\\overset{\\to }{ZY}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={45}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299820 13194139534630 true] [17592186299819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299821 13194139534630 true] [17592186299819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299822 13194139534630 true] [17592186299819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299823 13194139534630 true] [17592186299819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299824 13194139534630 true] [17592186299819 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534630 true] [17592186299819 1041 "selection" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299819 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299822 13194139534630 true] [17592186299819 1110 #uuid "3c26df84-5374-5583-8294-99ed982e65e9" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299820 1034 "{60}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299820 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299820 1111 #uuid "cc682e91-ae05-504d-a75b-61df41993129" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299821 1034 "{90}^{∘}" 13194139534630 true] [17592186299821 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534630 true] [17592186299821 1111 #uuid "22262f06-d52f-5b38-9f64-4a78a1175669" 131941395346